# CTRLO-OTHER-PICKERS: Ctrl-O over /fork's menu after three turns (the
# newest prompt marked), then one key at a time between a Ctrl-O and its
# return. Up first: the mark is on the last row.
# Then Ctrl-O and C-k, and Ctrl-O and C-j, each pair one `send-keys` of two
# bytes, so one burst: the screen is still up for the second byte, no picker
# takes it (routePickerControlByte, app_input_runtime.zig:1093-1116), and
# the composer's edit closes the menu (dismissActiveMenusForComposerEdit,
# :1984-1990) -- C-j leaving a new line (`burst-ck`, `burst-cj`).
# fx closes the full transcript before every frame while this menu is up
# (reconcileBeforeFrameRender, app_render_runtime.zig:1206-1215@481104fd), so
# Ctrl-O over it shows nothing and every key below is the menu's own, as
# without Ctrl-O: `held` is the composer's plane with the menu, C-j and C-k
# move the mark (routePickerControlByte, app_input_runtime.zig:1093-1116),
# Escape closes the menu (resolveEscape, :2765).
fx: env FX_AUTO_UPGRADE=0
gateway p5-effort-fork-turns.json
wait 3
type first prompt alpha
key Enter
wait 3
type second prompt beta
key Enter
wait 3
type third prompt gamma
key Enter
wait 3
type /fork
key Enter
wait 1
snap open
key C-o
wait 0.8
snap held
key C-o
wait 0.8
key C-o
wait 0.8
key Up
wait 0.4
key C-o
wait 0.8
snap up
key C-o
wait 0.8
key C-k
wait 0.4
key C-o
wait 0.8
snap ck
key C-o
wait 0.8
key C-j
wait 0.4
key C-o
wait 0.8
snap cj
key C-o
wait 0.8
key Tab
wait 0.4
key C-o
wait 0.8
snap tab
key C-o
wait 0.8
key Escape
wait 0.8
snap esc
type /fork
key Enter
wait 1
key Up
wait 0.4
key -H 0f 0b
wait 0.8
snap burst-ck
type /fork
key Enter
wait 1
key Up
wait 0.4
key -H 0f 0a
wait 0.8
snap burst-cj
